course: dictionary
lesson: 796
title: One word, two jobs: beep
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A beep is a short, high sound made by a machine, like a microwave, a car horn or a phone. Words like beep can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action). As a noun: «leave a message after the beep». As a verb: «beep the horn» means make the horn sound.
explain: Look at the words around beep to find its job. If it comes after a or the, as in «a beeping sound» or «after the beep», it is probably a noun. If it comes after a person or thing doing something, as in «beep the horn», it is a verb.
explain: A beep is a signal. It tells you that something needs your attention: the food is ready, the battery is low, or a door is open. When a smoke alarm beeps, you must tell an adult straight away.
fact: «Beep» is a noun (a beep, beeps) or a verb (beep, beeps, beeped, beeping).
fact: The past tense of beep is «beeped». Something that is beeping is making the sound right now.
fact: «Hospital machines monitor heart rate, oxygen and breathing and beep when something needs checking, which is often not urgent.» So a beep does not always mean danger.
fact: A beep is a signal: it tells you that something needs your attention.
fact: A car beeping at you is a warning, so listen and look around.
exercise: In «the doors beep to warn that they are closing», what does beep do? | Drives the bus away | Opens the doors slowly | *Makes a warning sound | Closes the windows
exercise: What does beeping mean in «tubes, wires and beeping machines»? | Machines that need to be painted | *Machines making a short, high sound | Machines that are very large | Machines that are broken and silent
exercise: «Leave a message after the beep.» What is beep in this sentence? | *A noun: a short, high sound | A kind of phone | A verb: to shout a message | A type of car
test: What is a beep most like? | A kind of food | A colour | *A signal that tells you something | A long song
test: A smoke alarm starts to beep. What should you do? | Ignore it, it is just a noise | Turn the sound up to hear it better | *Tell an adult straight away | Shout at it to stop
exam: A boy in Perth wore headphones and did not hear a truck's «beeping» while walking behind it. Why was this risky? | *The beep was a warning that the truck was reversing close by | Beeping is only a kind of music | Headphones make every sound louder | Trucks never beep, so nothing was wrong
